@page "/"

<PageTitle>RayCraft examples</PageTitle>

<section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
    <span class="eyebrow">Free controls · Examples</span>
    <h1 id="hero-title" class="hero__title">Examples<br /><em>that run</em></h1>
    <p class="hero__lead">Live examples with their source for the free controls of RayCraft.Blazor, @ControlCatalog.All.Count in all. Every page shows the parameters read from the package. The code of the library is not in this repository; it comes from the NuGet package.</p>
</section>

<section class="about" aria-labelledby="about-title">
    <h2 id="about-title" class="about__title">About RayCraft</h2>
    <div class="about__grid">
        <article>
            <h3>Who we are</h3>
            <p>RayCraft is a library of controls for Blazor, built by DiPiGi Ltd. It is meant for teams with in-house development and for freelance developers who want one consistent, accessible set of controls. More at <a href="https://raycraft.dev">raycraft.dev</a>.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
            <h3>What we do</h3>
            <p>RayCraft.Blazor is the free NuGet package: @ControlCatalog.All.Count controls for Blazor Server, WebAssembly and Auto. This site shows every one of them with a working example.</p>
            <p>RayCraft Full, with data grids, charts, scheduling, workspace, diagrams and Office controls, is coming soon.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
            <h3>What sets us apart</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Accessible by design: standard keyboard patterns, a visible focus, and a goal of WCAG 2.2 level AA.</li>
                <li>No third-party UI dependencies.</li>
                <li>Clear licenses: the package has its own license, these examples are MIT.</li>
            </ul>
        </article>
    </div>
    <p class="about__contact">Support: <a href="mailto:support@raycraft.dev">support@raycraft.dev</a>. Security reports: <a href="mailto:security@raycraft.dev">security@raycraft.dev</a>.</p>
</section>

<section class="getstarted" aria-labelledby="start-title">
    <h2 id="start-title" class="about__title">Use it in your project</h2>
    <pre tabindex="0"><code>dotnet add package RayCraft.Blazor

// Program.cs
builder.Services.AddRayCraft();

&lt;!-- App.razor, in the head and before the end of the body --&gt;
&lt;link rel="stylesheet" href="_content/RayCraft.Blazor/css/raycraft.css" /&gt;
&lt;script src="_content/RayCraft.Blazor/raycraft.js"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;

@@* _Imports.razor *@@
@@using RayCraft.Blazor.Components</code></pre>
    <p class="about__contact">Use an interactive render mode. <code>Program.cs</code> and <code>App.razor</code> of this site show all of it.</p>
</section>

